content:
### Why This Error Occurred

In [`contracts/src/index.ts`](file:///e:/keys-of-the-departed/contracts/src/index.ts#L205-L220), `CreateInvestigationInput` is defined using Zod:

```typescript
export const CreateInvestigationSchema = z
  .object({
    name: z.string().trim().min(1).max(120),
    description: z.string().trim().max(500).optional().default(""),
  })
  .strict();

export type CreateInvestigationInput = z.infer<typeof CreateInvestigationSchema>;
```

In Zod, **`z.infer<T>` infers the output type (`z.output<T>`)** of the parser, not the raw input type. Because `description` has `.default("")`, Zod guarantees that after parsing, `description` is always populated as a `string`. Consequently, TypeScript resolves `CreateInvestigationInput` to:

```typescript
{
  name: string;
  description: string; // required on the output type
}
```

In [`tests/db/mongodb.test.ts`](file:///e:/keys-of-the-departed/tests/db/mongodb.test.ts#L280-L282), `repo.createInvestigation` takes `CreateInvestigationInput`. The test passed an object literal directly without `description`:

```typescript
// ❌ Property 'description' is missing in '{ name: string }'
const inv = await repo.createInvestigation({
  name: "Rejection Audit",
});
```

---

### The Fix

The call in [`tests/db/mongodb.test.ts`](file:///e:/keys-of-the-departed/tests/db/mongodb.test.ts#L280-L283) has been updated to include `description`:

```typescript
// ✅ tests/db/mongodb.test.ts
const inv = await repo.createInvestigation({
  name: "Rejection Audit",
  description: "Enforces 5MB file size limit and allowed extensions",
});
```

All 11 tests in [`tests/db/mongodb.test.ts`](file:///e:/keys-of-the-departed/tests/db/mongodb.test.ts) pass with zero type errors.

*(Note: If you'd like callers to be able to omit `description` when invoking repository methods directly without TypeScript errors, [`contracts/src/index.ts`](file:///e:/keys-of-the-departed/contracts/src/index.ts#L220) could use `z.input<typeof CreateInvestigationSchema>` instead of `z.infer` for the input type).*

